d the size of a proposed old-growth timber sale in Tongass National Forest by 90%­ —protecting thousands of acres of habitat for wildlife like wolves, northern goshawks and brown and black bears.\n2018 DEFENDERS HIGHLIGHTS We released 27 scarlet macaws in the Los Tuxtlas Biosphere Reserve in Mexico, which now has the second-largest wild population of this highly imper"
